<BaseLayout title="SWEEP Academy Primary School" description="SWEEP Academy is an independent Christian primary school covering Grade R to Grade 7, with a loving, caring and disciplined environment grounded in Biblical principles.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container page-hero-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Primary school · Grade R–7</span><h1>SWEEP Academy <em style="color:var(--green-2);font-style:normal">Primary School</em></h1><p>Rock-solid education underpinned by remedial support and family values. SWEEP Academy supports your child through the fundamental stages of their educational journey.</p><a class="button" href="/admissions/">Ask about admissions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><img src={image} alt="SWEEP Academy Primary School, image from the existing school website" fetchpriority="high" /></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container content-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>Vision statement</h2><p>“For he shall be like a tree planted by the waters, and that spreads out its roots by the river, and shall not fear when the heat comes, but its leaf shall be green, and shall not be anxious in the year of drought, neither shall cease from yielding fruit.” — Jeremiah 17:8</p><p>We embrace excellence in education and offer a loving, caring and disciplined environment.</p><h2>Mission statement</h2><p>We promise to provide the highest quality education, care and supervision for all learners, with the goal of assisting them to grow, develop and achieve their true potential in spirit, soul and body, with sound Biblical principles as the foundation of their decision-making DNA.</p><h2>Scope and curriculum</h2><p>The existing website states that SWEEP Academy follows the CAPS Curriculum from Grade R to Grade 3 and the IMPAC Curriculum from Grade 4 to Grade 7. This curriculum information must be confirmed as current before launch.</p><p>The listed subjects include Numeracy, Literacy (English, Afrikaans and Zulu), Science, Social Studies and Bible Study. The site also references detailed progress reports at the end of each term, age-appropriate computer studies, physical development, and a Performing Arts and Culture programme.</p><h2>Extra-mural activities</h2><p>The existing website references Dance Mouse, Dance Madness, DM Ballerina, swimming, Soccer Starz and Technokids computer training. Current availability, providers, age ranges and schedules require confirmation.</p><h2>Operating times</h2><p>The public website lists school hours as 07:30–13:45 on Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday, and 07:30–14:30 on Wednesday due to sports training. These times must be confirmed before publication.</p><h2>School term dates · 2026</h2><p>The existing public website lists the dates below. They are included here as source-reference information only and must be confirmed by the school before publication.</p><table class="term-table"><caption>Published 2026 term dates (pending confirmation)</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Term</th><th scope="col">Dates</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Term 1</th><td>14 January – 27 March 2026</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Term 2</th><td>8 April – 26 June 2026</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Term 3</th><td>21 July – 23 September 2026</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Term 4</th><td>6 October – 11 December 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="info-card"><h3>School details</h3><p><strong>Grades</strong><br />Grade R to Grade 7 (as described on the existing website)</p><p><strong>Telephone</strong><br /><a href="tel:+27116805938">011 680 5938</a></p><p><strong>Email</strong><br /><a href="mailto:schools@sweeplife.co.za">schools@sweeplife.co.za</a></p><p class="muted">Curriculum, operating times and contact details are pending school confirmation.</p><a class="button" href="/admissions/">Admissions enquiry <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside></div></section>
